//! `removeNode(p); removeNode(p->next);` relies on that. We reproduce the
//! model exactly with a `Vec<Node>` arena and `usize` handles: a handle is
//! never invalidated, so identity comparisons (`p != ear.prev`) and reads of
//! unlinked nodes behave as they do in C++.

